text:
rachel: Quick a11y note from a keyboard + SR pass on the models page (virtualized list + details panel). Two new-ish issues: when rows are virtualized the focus sometimes disappears after opening/closing details, and VoiceOver sometimes announces the wrong model name when virtualization re-renders. Posting quick repros and suggestions.

noel: Thanks. Repro steps? I haven't seen the VO name swap locally.

rachel: Repro on staging: tab to list, ArrowDown to a row (row gets focused), press Enter to open details panel. While panel is open, the list virtualizer unmounts offscreen rows. Press Esc to close. Expected: focus returns to the original row. Observed: focus lands on document.body or header; sometimes the focused row was unmounted and focusable id no longer exists.

mei: I can reproduce on mac+VO and NVDA. Also noticed: when virtualizer recycles the DOM, VO sometimes reads the next row's name instead of the selected one after closing. Feels like timing between focus restore and re-render.

a11y-bot: Automated hints: avoid restoring focus to an element that may be unmounted. Consider a focus-anchor pattern: insert a temporary focusable element at the logical list position, move focus to it on open, and restore focus to it on close; then remove it when stable. Also ensure the row toggle has stable ids and aria-controls pointing to the panel.

noel: Good call. Proposed approach: create an invisible but reachable focus anchor (tabindex=-1 but programmatically focusable) placed as a sibling to the list item. On open, call anchor.focus(); when closing, focus the anchor so we never target a removed node. Pseudocode: 

```
// create anchor near the row
const anchor = document.createElement('span');
anchor.id = `focus-anchor-${rowId}`;
anchor.tabIndex = -1;
row.parentNode.insertBefore(anchor, row.nextSibling);
anchor.focus({preventScroll:true});
// on close
anchor.focus();
// cleanup when stable
anchor.remove();
```

rachel: That should fix the unmount problem. Also: ensure aria-live announcements for open/close are deterministic. Right now toasts and the panel each have role=status which creates multiple polite announcements and out-of-order reads. We should centralize to a single live region for system messages and explicit panel open/close announcements (eg "Opened details for Model X").

mei: My validation checklist: keyboard-only open/close, focus anchor survives virtualization, VO/NVDA read correct model name after close, and single live region handles messages. I'll run tests after PR.

noel: I'll convert the row toggle to a proper <button> with aria-expanded + aria-controls, add stable ids, and implement the focus-anchor utility in the virtualized list component. I'll also remove role=status from the panel and use a single status region for toasts and panel announcements.

rachel: Small visual/accessibility tweak: focus-visible halo for the virtualized rows is pretty subtle on compact dark rows. Recommend 3px high-contrast ring and avoid relying on box-shadow alone.

noel: Will use outline: 3px solid token('--focus') + outline-offset: 3px. I'll include dark/light checks.

a11y-bot: After changes run automated checks for: focusable elements not removed on blur, duplicate live regions, and stable id usage for aria-controls.

mei: Sounds good. Please tag me on the PR and I'll run NVDA + VO matrix.

rachel: Owners: Noel (implementation), Mei (validation), Rachel (acceptance criteria). Acceptance: focus anchor prevents focus loss, VO/NVDA announce correct model names, single live region for announcements, and focus halo passes contrast. Thanks!
